From: lfdevs <lfdevs@lfdevs.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 04:24:19 +0800
Subject: backend: clarify Anland service lifetimes

Describe the PipeWire and camera resource ownership as it is implemented by the wlroots backend, without referring to compositor-specific KWin lifecycle details.
---
 backend/anland/anland_audio.h  | 2 +-
 backend/anland/anland_camera.h | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/backend/anland/anland_audio.h b/backend/anland/anland_audio.h
index 7412cd6..9cdd6a0 100644
--- a/backend/anland/anland_audio.h
+++ b/backend/anland/anland_audio.h
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
  * Producer-side audio engine.
  *
  * Owns a persistent PipeWire thread-loop with two streams that live for the whole
- * KWin session, independent of whether a consumer is connected:
+ * compositor session, independent of whether a consumer is connected:
  *
  *   - a sink-monitor capture stream  -> desktop playback PCM written to the audio
  *                                        socket (heard on the Android speaker);
diff --git a/backend/anland/anland_camera.h b/backend/anland/anland_camera.h
index ad940c3..e18bee3 100644
--- a/backend/anland/anland_camera.h
+++ b/backend/anland/anland_camera.h
@@ -22,8 +22,8 @@
  * STOP_RECORD when the last consumer goes away). Frames arrive in the layout announced
  * by each stream_fd and are emitted by that camera's Video/Source.
  *
- * All fds passed to set_resources are OWNED by the engine (SCM_RIGHTS dups) and closed
- * in clear()/stop().
+ * All fds passed to set_resources are transferred to the engine and closed in
+ * clear()/stop().
  */
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
